    "body": "@ramonpetgrave64 thank you for the suggestion. Our current recommendation is to use the [OPA policy engine] (https://www.openpolicyagent.org/docs/latest/) for these types of use cases. For your use case, we could use the [OPA CLI](https://www.openpolicyagent.org/docs/latest/cli/) with `gh` like this:\n\n```\ncat <<EOF > super_secure_policy.rego\npackage artifact.attestations\n\nimport future.keywords.every\n\ndefault source_repo_ref_verification = false\n\nsource_repo_ref_verification {\n    every bundle in input {\n        bundle.verificationResult.signature.certificate.sourceRepositoryRef == \"refs/heads/main\"\n    }\n}\nEOF\n\ngh attestation verify my-artifact  --bundle my-bundles.jsonl -o my-org --format json | opa eval --stdin-input --data super_secure_policy.rego \"data.artifact.attestations.source_repo_ref_verification\"\n```",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
