    "body": "@malancas Thansk for replying. I could consider using OPA, but it seems very heavyweight, since the CLI almost has support for what I'm requesting, especially around jq.\r\n\r\nPerhaps you could consider adding another option `--jq-exit-status`, where it evaluates the truthy statements from the existing `--jq` query and exits non-zero if false.\r\n\r\nTurning this pipe to the `jq` command\r\n\r\n```\r\ngh attestation verify ... --format json| jq --exit-status 'select(.[].verificationResult.signature.certificate.sourceRepositoryRef=\"refs/heads/main\")\r\n```\r\n\r\ninto\r\n\r\n```\r\ngh attestation verify ... --jq-exit-status --jq 'select(.[].verificationResult.signature.certificate.sourceRepositoryRef==\"refs/heads/main\")' \r\n```\r\n\r\nMore conditionals for other attestation properties can be [combined](https://jqlang.github.io/jq/manual/#and-or-not) with `and`.",
