    "body": "Hi @ramonpetgrave64! Sorry for the delay in getting back to you.\n\nSo what I'm hearing is:\n- For you, it's not good enough to be able to validate that an artifact it came from a given repository\n- You're concerned someone may have signed an artifact but from a non-protected branch\n- But there's more information in there, could we not let you verify that the commit sha is what you expect?\n\nIn other words, your threat model includes people who might have access to the repo but not to the default/protected branch.\n\nTwo questions for you.\n\n1) Are you envisioning that:\n- `--commit` would apply to `.verificationResults.signature.sourceRepositoryDigest`\n- `--ref` would apply to `.verificationResults.signature.sourceRepositoryRef`\n\n2) How are you propagating the correct commit sha to your verification environment? We've shied away from this level of granularity simply because it seemed unlikely for _most people_ to readily be able to specify it.\n\n---\n\nWe're about to do some work polishing verification and I'll bring this up for discussion with the team 😄 .",
